From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:59:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ldc pilot): lr-0 cells declare their behaviour UNDEFINED
 in the artifact (RULING T1-lr0)

A learning-off cell's success sits at chance by design; each per-race score dict
holds two gate arms with success <= acc_among_responders, so a chance-level cell
reads 'every arm below 0.5' about half the time. The runner now writes
behavior_verdict UNDEFINED (lr 0 diagnostic) for lr 0 runs, and --declare-lr0
adds the same declaration to records written before it (refuses lr > 0, changes
no measured value, records the declaring runner sha256). Pinned by
tests/test_ldc_pilot_lr0_declaration.py, failing-first on the T1 record shape.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YFsTogbFUHqkhjUeERc6a5
